small changes:
[x] feed: empty state while a channel filter is active didn't say so
    -> found while testing the chip fixes above: filtering to a channel with
       nothing left in the queue showed the generic "All caught up" message,
       which reads as "nothing anywhere" - easy to forget a filter is still
       on and wonder why posts stopped showing up. Added a distinct empty
       state for this case (feed_screen.dart) - "No posts in {channel}" +
       a "Clear filter" button that resets selectedChannelFilterProvider -
       shown only when posts are empty AND a channel filter is active, so it
       doesn't shadow the real "nothing to review anywhere" case. New
       strings in both app_en.arb/app_de.arb.
[x] custom server selection should be only available in the app and not in the web version
[x] register route should not allow to set is_superuser or is verified
    -> the field is not actually set in backend but should not be available in the FE
[x] the web version, but with large screen should get a disclaimer banner that the app is the preferred and a link to the app store (placeholder for now)
[ ] introduce new app naming
[x] check if user can only get and interact with posts that are in his feed @done
    -> review (forward/drop) was already safe (claim_from_queue checks queue membership).
       GET /posts/{id} was not: it only checked channel subscription, so any subscriber
       could view any post in the channel by guessing its id. Fixed to require the post
       be in the user's queue, already reviewed by them, or authored by them.
