features:
[x] a post must support images and videos @done
    -> in-DB storage (like profile pics), up to 5 images/videos per post, 40MB
       combined. Images: Pillow re-encodes + strips EXIF/GPS + downscales,
       server-derives content_type (never trusts the client). Video: ffmpeg/
       ffprobe probe duration and re-mux to strip container metadata (GPS
       included) without a full transcode - new backend dependency, added to
       the Dockerfile. New PostMedia table; POST /posts is now multipart;
       GET /posts/{id}/media/{id} reuses the same _can_view_post gate as the
       post itself (stricter than the profile-picture route) and supports
       HTTP Range so video_player can stream/scrub instead of downloading the
       whole clip first. App: feed card shows a real thumbnail (+N badge for
       extra items, neutral play-icon tile for video - no frame extraction),
       detail sheet gets a swipeable gallery with chewie-based playback,
       composer gets photo/video pickers with a preview strip.
[x] post creation view is crowded and can be organized more space efficiently @done
